# store deploy — copy to .env. TLS is terminated by the deployment environment.
#
# NOTE: nothing here configures the CONNECTOR any more. Since the cutover to the
# Rust connector (connector#755) there is no environment-variable layer on that
# side at all — every connector value comes from ./connector.toml, and its two
# secrets are FILES you generate next to it (see README.md). What remains below
# configures the store app, the image pins, and the published port.

# ── Identities ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED: store Nostr identity. Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
STORE_NOSTR_SECRET_KEY=
#
# The connector's identities are NOT here. `TOON_MNEMONIC` used to derive the
# settlement key at boot and no longer does anything:
#   deploy/signer.key      — fresh random, this node's ILP identity, holds no money
#   deploy/settlement.key  — derived at NIP-06 m/44'/1237'/0'/0/0, spends value
# Both are gitignored and mounted read-only into the container.
#
# The old note here said this identity also funded the store box's own
# kind:10032 self-announce. It does not: the always-on `selfAnnounce` timer is
# gone for good, and this settlement key isn't wired to any replacement — the
# Rust connector's `[announce]` section + one-shot `connector announce` verb
# exist on this bundle's pinned tag, but `connector.toml` doesn't configure
# them. See README.md.

# ── Arweave wallet ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# base64(JSON RSA JWK) of a funded Arweave wallet. Empty → ephemeral free-tier
# (≤100KB uploads, no deposit; the ephemeral key rotates on every restart).
STORE_ARWEAVE_JWK_B64=
# Flat per-job fee (base units). Informational only — the connector enforces the
# flat route price in connector.toml, which is what a payer is actually charged.
FEE_PER_JOB=10

# ── Images ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The connector image baked into store-connector. Pin an exact `rust-sha-` tag,
# never the floating `rust-main`: the config parser is `deny_unknown_fields` and
# startup is fail-closed, so a schema drift is a refuse-to-start.
#
# The `connector` package holds BOTH lineages under one name. A plain semver tag
# (`3.28.0`, `latest`) is the RETIRED TypeScript node, which reads YAML and will
# not start on ./connector.toml. Only `rust-*` tags are this connector.
CONNECTOR_TAG=rust-sha-440eab7
# The published store-connector image (prod: pin a tag and `up` without --build).
STORE_CONNECTOR_IMAGE=ghcr.io/toon-protocol/store-connector:latest
# The published store app image.
STORE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/toon-protocol/store:latest

# ── Ports ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
EDGE_PORT=3000
